.TH BOSWAS-ANDROID 1 "November 2026" "boswas-android 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-android \- manage the Android runtime and Android apps on Boswas OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-android
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-android
manages the optional Android runtime of Boswas OS (Waydroid, LineageOS
without Google applications) and the Android apps in it. It runs as the
desktop user. Steps that change the system (installing, setting up, updating,
repairing or removing the runtime, starting or stopping its container service)
are performed by
.B /usr/libexec/boswas/sysops
through
.BR pkexec (1),
which asks for authorisation.
.PP
The runtime is installed only when a user asks for it and never starts on its
own; Android apps never start automatically.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Runtime installation and version, compatibility checks, whether the runtime is
set up, Android image type and versions, container service, session, storage,
network (waydroid0), graphics acceleration, and the Google Play assessment.
.TP
.B check
Only the compatibility checks: binder driver, Wayland session, processor,
kernel, graphics, free disk space and Secure Boot (PASS, WARN, FAIL, UNKNOWN).
.TP
.BI "apk inspect " FILE
Describe an APK without running anything from it: package, name, version,
SDK levels, native ABIs, split status, signing schemes and signer certificate
SHA-256 fingerprints, and whether it can run here. Inspection does not show
that an app is safe.
.TP
.BI "apk install " FILE
Inspect, then install into the running Android session. APKs with native code
only for ARM processors and split APKs are refused with an explanation.
APKs are never modified or re-signed; Android verifies the signature.
.TP
.B app list
Installed Android apps (package and name).
.TP
.BI "app launch " PACKAGE
Start an app (starts Android if needed).
.TP
.BI "app remove " PACKAGE
Uninstall an app; its launcher entry is removed.
.TP
.BR "session start" | stop
Start or stop Android for this user.
.TP
.BR "runtime install" | init | update | repair | "remove " [ \-\-purge\-data ]
Install Waydroid from its signed repository, download and verify the Android
images (init), update them, repair the runtime, or remove it
.RB ( \-\-purge\-data
also deletes the images). Prints the progress of boswas-sysops; "cancel" on
standard input or the first Ctrl+C cancels while nothing has been changed yet.
.TP
.BR "service start" | stop | restart
The Android container service.
.TP
.B fdroid install
Download the F-Droid client over HTTPS, require F-Droid's published signing
certificate, and install it. F-Droid is an independent catalogue of free and
open-source apps; it is not Google Play.
.TP
.B google-play
Why Google Play is not available on Boswas OS, and the alternatives.
.TP
.BI "logs " "\fR[\fP" "\-\-lines " "N\fR]\fP"
The Boswas Android log and the Waydroid log.
.TP
.BR cleanup " [" \-\-yes ]
After the runtime was removed: delete your Android data and leftover Android
launcher entries.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print JSON (schema boswas-android/1); the runtime and service commands print
the JSON Lines of boswas-sysops. Errors are printed as
{"schema", "error": {"code", "message", "problems"}}.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 done; 1 failed; 2 invalid argument or refused (incompatible APK, confirmation
missing); 3 runtime not installed, not set up or not running; 6 this computer or
session cannot run the runtime. The runtime and service commands exit with the
status of boswas-sysops (126 or 127: not authorised).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/boswas/android/runtime.conf
Where the runtime comes from (repository, key fingerprint, allowed packages,
image type, F-Droid URL and certificate).
.TP
.I /usr/share/boswas/keyrings/waydroid.gpg
The Waydroid repository signing key.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/boswas/android.log
This command's own log.
.TP
.I /var/lib/waydroid/waydroid.log
The Waydroid log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1)
